    <briefdescription>
<para>Fast scoring of Particles against electron microscopy class averages. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The restraint fits the particles into the 2D images by alignment of principal components of each of the particles&apos; projections with principal components of the 2D class average. Therefore, the particle set should comprise all subunits that are in the image. The aligned projections are scored against 2D class averages using the cross correlation score. This is a fast alignment and score that works well for negative stain EM class averages. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
